** ==========================================================================
** calculix_uniaxial_bar.inp — transcribed CalculiX/Abaqus deck, EXACT answer.
** A prismatic bar of 4 C3D8 hexes along x, cross-section 1 x 1 (consistent
** units). Left face (x=0) fixed in x; a y,z pin removes rigid body motion.
** Right face (x=4) pulled with a total axial force F = 1000 (250 per node).
**   exact:  sigma_xx = F / A = 1000 / 1 = 1000        (uniform)
**           tip u_x  = sigma * L / E = 1000 * 4 / 210e9 = 1.90476e-8
** This is a constant-stress field a valid element reproduces to machine eps,
** so CalculiX and Forge must agree to round-off.
